WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.130
Flat land by the sea.

2
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.100
A huge sky.

3
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.100
A long sea wall holds back the water.

4
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.570
A church tower on a low mound.

5
00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:13.290
And between two poles,
a single telegraph wire.

6
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.780
The wind blows across the marsh,
and the wire begins to hum.

7
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.150
Sea, sky and sunset, and a wire.

8
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.360
So why put a telegraph wire in the poem?

9
00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.760
In this mission, you'll
visit Romney Marsh,

10
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:32.080
on the Kent coast, guarded from
the sea by the Dymchurch Wall.

11
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.790
You'll walk with John Davidson's
speaker to the sea wall and back,

12
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.880
from sunset into night.

13
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.250
And you'll listen to the
poem's sounds: the wind,

14
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.320
the wire and the sea.

15
00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.090
Your mission: explain why
the wire is in the poem.
